{"id":"4429795","slug":"jahmyr-gibbs","name":"Jahmyr Gibbs","position":"RB","team":"DET","headshot":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/headshots/nfl/players/full/4429795.png","formats":{"ppr-12":{"positionRank":1,"ourRank":1,"vorRound":1,"adp":1.4,"projected":242.5281482708899,"vor":144.73233537450477,"expectedGames":10.045046585715268,"floor":null,"median":null,"ceiling":null,"tier":1,"preseasonRank":5,"preseasonPoints":262.1},"half-ppr-12":{"positionRank":1,"ourRank":1,"vorRound":1,"adp":1.5,"projected":226.47502558120794,"vor":143.91029500572853,"expectedGames":10.045046585715268,"floor":null,"median":null,"ceiling":null,"tier":1,"preseasonRank":6,"preseasonPoints":254.35},"standard-12":{"positionRank":1,"ourRank":1,"vorRound":1,"adp":1.5,"projected":196.34929732716128,"vor":128.53584712898936,"expectedGames":10.045046585715268,"floor":null,"median":null,"ceiling":null,"tier":1,"preseasonRank":3,"preseasonPoints":227.66}},"capsule":{"body":"The receiving jump is what separates Gibbs from every other back near the top of drafts. His target share went from 12.1% in 2024 to 17.1% last season, RB4 among qualifying backs, and 613 receiving yards came with it. That's the kind of role that holds up even on weeks when the run game stalls. He scored above the position's weekly median in 16 of 17 games and cleared 15 points in 11 of them. Only Bijan Robinson finished one spot ahead of him.\n\nThe usage backs it up. A 67.1% snap share ranks RB9, John Morton and Dan Campbell are both back, and the red-zone work is real in volume terms: 67 red-zone touches, RB3, one spot behind Jonathan Taylor. The odd part is that red-zone touches were only 19.9% of his own touches, RB36 among qualifying backs, so Detroit spreads the carries near the goal line and his scoring leans on the passing game and big plays. His best week, 55.4 points in week 12, tells you how the ceiling arrives.\n\nWe project him at 262 points, about 20 more than backs drafted at his ADP of 1.4 have historically returned, and his middle range runs 218 to 307. That's well short of last year's 366.6, which is fine, it's still RB1 on our board with a 16-point cliff behind him and only two tier-mates before the drop. The games question is the one real risk: we expect 15, with a range of 9 to 17, and he has played 34 of 34 the past two years. Take him first overall and don't think twice.","pulls":[{"figure":"262","caption":"projected PPR points"},{"figure":"16","caption":"PPR points to the next tier"},{"figure":"1.4","caption":"his ADP in PPR drafts"}]},"season":{"season":2026,"format":"ppr-12","weeks":18,"through":5,"games":5,"pointsPerGame":30.7,"totals":{"pass_attempts":0.0,"completions":0.0,"passing_yards":0.0,"passing_touchdowns":0.0,"interceptions":0.0,"carries":105.0,"rushing_yards":504.0,"rushing_touchdowns":7.0,"targets":34.0,"receptions":27.0,"receiving_yards":243.0,"receiving_touchdowns":2.0,"fumbles_lost":1.0,"field_goals_made":0.0,"extra_points_made":0.0,"sacks":0.0,"defensive_interceptions":0.0,"defensive_touchdowns":0.0,"snapShare":0.7674418604651163,"points":153.7},"log":[{"pass_attempts":0.0,"completions":0.0,"passing_yards":0.0,"passing_touchdowns":0.0,"interceptions":0.0,"carries":29.0,"rushing_yards":156.0,"rushing_touchdowns":2.0,"targets":5.0,"receptions":5.0,"receiving_yards":30.0,"receiving_touchdowns":0.0,"fumbles_lost":1.0,"field_goals_made":0.0,"extra_points_made":0.0,"sacks":0.0,"defensive_interceptions":0.0,"defensive_touchdowns":0.0,"snapShare":0.7402597402597403,"points":33.6,"week":1,"opponent":"NO","home":true,"status":"played"},{"pass_attempts":0.0,"completions":0.0,"passing_yards":0.0,"passing_touchdowns":0.0,"interceptions":0.0,"carries":16.0,"rushing_yards":52.0,"rushing_touchdowns":0.0,"targets":8.0,"receptions":6.0,"receiving_yards":61.0,"receiving_touchdowns":1.0,"fumbles_lost":0.0,"field_goals_made":0.0,"extra_points_made":0.0,"sacks":0.0,"defensive_interceptions":0.0,"defensive_touchdowns":0.0,"snapShare":0.8307692307692308,"points":23.3,"week":2,"o